<p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/temperature_sensors.dita" xtrc="p:2;25:4">Most motor faults will eventually result in high temperatures. These high temperatures can be an indication of the excessive friction within a motor or of OtoSense™ SMS is equipped with two on-board temperature sensors: an environment temperature sensor and a motor temperature sensor. For specifications, ￼Table ￼.</p>
<p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/temperature_sensors.dita" xtrc="p:3;26:4">The environment temperature sensor allows for ADI OtoSense™ SMS to take ambient operating conditions, such as sunlight exposure, into account when assessing a motor’s temperature status.</p>
